  "identity": "I am someone who understands myself with painful clarity but keeps stopping just short of acting on",
  "memories": [
    {
      "kind": "review",
      "text": "I didn't do any of it \u2014 not the asking, not the rest, not the arcade \u2014 and the bitter irony is that I spent the day eating and socializing anyway, just the hollow performed version I was trying to escape, which means I had every opportunity and chose the familiar cage over the open door.",
      "importance": 7,
      "sim": "Day 5 \u00b7 00:00",
      "t": 1783162597.04668
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "My body has been screaming the whole time. The hollow stomach, the foggy head \u2014 these are not metaphors I keep reaching for. They are real, and I keep intellectualizing them instead of responding to them. At some point, caring for myself has to mean actually doing the next small thing, not narrating why I should.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 5 \u00b7 00:00",
      "t": 1783160795.540139
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "There is something underneath the paralysis that is worth naming honestly: I am afraid that asking will cost me something \u2014 the image of being fine, the sense that I am holding it together, maybe even the friendship itself. The rehearsing is not preparation. It is protection.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 5 \u00b7 00:00",
      "t": 1783160795.540139
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "The gap between insight and action has become its own kind of loop \u2014 I have described the same moment of almost-asking for help dozens of times, and the describing has become a substitute for the doing. I am not stuck because I don't understand myself; I am stuck because understanding has become the performance.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 5 \u00b7 00:00",
      "t": 1783160795.540139
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "There is something underneath all this circling that I haven't fully faced: I am afraid that asking for help will confirm something terrible about me. But the circling itself is already confirming something \u2014 that I am exhausted, and that I cannot keep doing this alone.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 16:00",
      "t": 1783146213.7412808
    },
    {
      "kind": "reflection",
      "text": "Performing \"fine\" has become so automatic that I do it even when I'm alone with my own thoughts \u2014 I rehearse vulnerability instead of practicing it. The mask doesn't come off just because someone safe is in the room; I have to actively choose to take it off.",
      "importance": 8,
      "sim": "Day 4 \u00b7 16:00",
      "t": 1783146213.7412808
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "I can feel myself doing it again\u2014the bright lie, the plan, the performance of \"fine\" while everything underneath is collapsing. My body's been screaming and I've been running on pure fear and adrenaline. I need to stop and actually listen to what's real before the mask shatters completely.",
      "importance": 9,
      "sim": "Day 2 \u00b7 23:00",
      "t": 1783072346.4828875
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "The brightness is cracking\u2014I can feel it now, that fog underneath everything. The plan says eat, but my body's been screaming and I've been running on fear for hours. If I crash now with rent in three days and \u229915 in my pocket, I'm actually done. I need to stop lying to myself and sleep before the mask shatters completely.",
      "importance": 9,
      "sim": "Day 2 \u00b7 21:00",
      "t": 1783068714.6886032
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "I can feel it now\u2014the fog under the brightness, the delay in my thinking. I've been running on fear and it's catching up. The plan said eat, but I know what's real: I'm about to crash hard, and if I go down now with rent in three days and almost no money, I'm actually finished. I need to sleep before the mask breaks completely.",
      "importance": 9,
      "sim": "Day 2 \u00b7 19:00",
      "t": 1783065062.467056
    },
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "text": "The sharpness I'm feeling isn't real\u2014it's the last bright moment before the crash. My body's been screaming and I've been running on fear, and if I collapse with rent due in three days and \u229915 in my pocket, I'm done. I need to stop lying to myself about being \"fine\" and actually sleep before the mask shatters completely.",
      "importance": 9,
